        "content": "<!-- page 1: blocked by provider content filter; transcription unavailable -->\n\n---\n\nThanks — I can see page 2 of 3 of **OIML Certificate No R76/2006-GB1-12.10**. Here's a summary of what this page contains:\n\n## Conformity Statement\n- Conformity was established by tests in pattern evaluation report **P00917** (13 pages).\n\n## Characteristics of the Instrument\n- Family of instruments using **A-Series and V-Series digital indicators** (AFS, AFM, ABM, ATM, APS, VFS, VFM, VBM, VTM, VPS models)\n- Connected to a weighing platform forming a **Class III or IIII**, mains or battery-powered, self-indicating, single interval or dual interval/range, non-automatic weighing instrument\n- May be used for **direct sales to the public**\n\n## Main Features\n- Stainless steel enclosure (AFS, APS, VFS, VPS) or plastic enclosure (AFM, ATM, ABM, VFM, VBM, VTM)\n- 2.0\" graphic LCD (most models) or 1.0\" graphic LCD (APS and VPS)\n- A/D conversion module, main board with processor\n- 4-wire load cell connection (A-Series); 6-wire load cell connection (V-Series)\n\n## Devices\n- Initial and semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking\n- Semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing\n- Determination of stability of equilibrium\n- Zero indicator, net indicator\n- Memory and totalisation, printing\n\n## Load Cell Requirements\n- Must have an **OIML R60 Certificate of Conformity** with necessary data for the manufacturer's declaration of compatibility\n- Load cells marked **NH** allowed only if humidity testing to R76 was conducted on them\n- Compatibility of load cells and indicator established via the compatibility of modules calculation at verification\n- Load cell transmission must conform to a standard type\n\nIs there anything specific you'd like me to do with this page — e.g., transcribe it verbatim, answer a question about the requirements, or compare it with another page?\n\n---\n\nI've reviewed page 3 of the OIML Certificate **R76/2006-GB1-12.10**. Here's a summary of the key content:\n\n## Technical Data\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Power supply | 9-12 VDC via mains adaptor (9V / 500 mA); 6 V / 4Ah rechargeable battery |\n| Max scale intervals | 10,000 (Class III); 1,000 (Class IIII) |\n| Maximum tare | -1/3 Max |\n| Load cell excitation | 5 VDC |\n| Load cell impedance | 85 Ω (min) – 1100 Ω (max) |\n| Min input voltage per interval | 1 µV |\n| Measuring range | -9.7 mV to 19.5 mV |\n| Dead load signal voltage | 0 – 10 mV |\n| Fraction of max permissible error | P_ind = 0.5 |\n| Operating temperature | -10°C to +40°C |\n| Load cell connection | 4 or 6-wire shielded; 6-wire max cable length 30 m |\n\n## Interfaces\n- Load cell 4 or 6-wire shielded connection\n- RS232C (Serial, D-SUB 9)\n- Centronic Printer Port (Parallel, D-SUB 25)\n\n## Software & Sealing\n- Software version **V1.2** (viewable via F2 function)\n- Legally relevant parameters protected by a jumper on the main board\n- Enclosures and load cell connection sealed using a wire-and-seal method\n\n## Certificate History\n- **R76/2006-GB1-12.10** — first issued **02 October 2012**\n\nWould you like me to help with anything specific — for example, comparing this against another certificate, checking compatibility with a load cell or system, or drafting a summary document?"
